From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 09:37:53 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] xsettings: Mirror to the GNOME settings only under Caminito

Caminito, the Wayland compositor for MATE, is the XSETTINGS manager of its
XWayland server: it has to keep Xft/DPI and Gdk/WindowScalingFactor in
step with its X11 scale, and to publish the settings again each time
XWayland starts. The plugin found that owner of _XSETTINGS_S0 and stopped
with "You can only run one xsettings manager at a time".

Native Wayland applications get nothing from XSETTINGS in any case. GTK
reads org.gnome.desktop.interface, .peripherals.mouse, .wm.preferences and
.sound there, and never an org.mate key, so they ignored the theme, fonts
and cursor set in the control center.

When MATE_WM_NAME is Caminito, do not take _XSETTINGS_S0, and start only a
mirror: it copies MATE's settings one way into those GNOME keys, at
start-up and on every change, and writes a key only when its value
differs. That also leaves out the X resources and the QT_SCALE_FACTOR
export, which are wrong on Wayland. Without that variable, nothing changes.

MATE has no light or dark key, so the apps that read the colour scheme
from the portal (browsers, Electron and libadwaita apps) stayed light with
a dark theme. The mirror also works out org.gnome.desktop.interface
color-scheme from the GTK theme: prefer-dark when the theme's window
background is darker than its text, and default otherwise.
